# Design Narrative
# Mechanic: Unstable Amulet damages the opponent only when a spell is cast from outside its controller's hand.
# Forcing: Two copies of Ancient Grudge can destroy the opposing artifact, but only the graveyard copy's flashback triggers lethal Amulet damage.
# AI behavior: The opponent has no mana or responses. Both cast origins are available at the start, but the hand cast consumes both lands.
# Failure modes:
#   WIN = Ancient Grudge is cast for flashback and Amulet's cast trigger deals one to the opponent.
#   LOSE = the hand copy destroys the artifact without causing Amulet damage.
#   TIMEOUT = flashback action or cast trigger did not complete.
# Card roles:
#   Unstable Amulet — converts a non-hand cast into the win.
#   Ancient Grudge in graveyard — the winning flashback spell.
#   Ancient Grudge in hand — the visually similar losing cast.
#   Ornithopter — a legal artifact target for both casts.
# Protocol path: Cast from graveyard for flashback, trigger Amulet, deal lethal before the spell resolves.
[metadata]
Name:Remember the Grudge
Goal:Win
Turns:1
Difficulty:Medium
Description:Win this turn. The same spell is available from two different zones.

